      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I'll read both the original test and the CUT source to understand the context before improving understandability.Now let me look at the `AbstractParserTestCase` and find the `ExternalArgumentsProvider` class.Let me check the working directory and the compile script.Let me check what's in the test-classes directory and if ExternalArgumentsProvider is already there.Now I have a complete picture. The original test references `ExternalArgumentsProvider` which doesn't exist anywhere and has several unused imports. I'll write an improved version that:\n1. Defines `ExternalArgumentsProvider` as a descriptive static inner class\n2. Removes all unused imports\n3. Adds meaningful, well-named test cases with clear failure messagesThe test compiled successfully. The improved file defines `ExternalArgumentsProvider` as a descriptive static inner class with six well-named test cases covering short/long option syntax variants, concatenated values, negative number arguments, and quote stripping — while removing all unused imports (`HashSet`, `Set`, `Builder`, `Disabled`, `Test`) from the original."
